    "details": "The OpenResty developers report:\n\n> The nginx core was upgraded from nginx 1.31.1 to 1.31.8, which\n> incorporates 12 CVE fixes, grouped by the first fixed version: 1.31.2:\n> HTTP/3 use-after-free (CVE-2026-42530), HTTP/2 and gRPC upstream\n> buffer overflow (CVE-2026-42055), and charset conversion buffer\n> overread (CVE-2026-48142); 1.31.3: buffer overflow involving map and\n> regex (CVE-2026-42533), memory disclosure involving slice or\n> background cache updates (CVE-2026-60005), and SSI use-after-free\n> (CVE-2026-56434); 1.31.6: HTTP/3 heap buffer overflow with certain\n> OpenSSL versions and configurations (CVE-2026-90439); 1.31.7: buffer\n> overflow involving alias and rewrite (CVE-2026-15176), buffer overflow\n> during variable expression evaluation (CVE-2026-93479), HTTP/3 request\n> body injection (CVE-2026-95101), TLS session ticket forgery\n> (CVE-2026-97629), and AIO and SSI use-after-free (CVE-2026-97205).\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0565",
